# wfg-log 1
# fixture undo — an edit taken back, put back, and refused twice.
#
# PR 5.4 named this file and PR 5.4 did not write it. §14.9 has said since that
# it pins the undo records; it did not, and the gap was found by an audit of
# what Phase 5 still owed (2026-09-16). This is that fixture, written the way
# the others were: by hand, and checked by hand.
#
# WHAT IT PINS, which no other test does. `undo` and `redo` are ordinary logged
# commands, and what they answer with is the whole of the guarantee: the domain
# they moved and the NAME of the transaction they moved. A replay rebuilds its
# own stack from the same inputs - the transaction hook is installed by `replay`
# as well as by `serve`, and the coalescing window keys on the address, the
# origin and the tick, all three of which are in this file - so a stack that
# drifted by one would answer with a different name and this fixture would fail
# on that record, with both names on screen. The unit suite asserts the stack;
# only a log can assert what the stack SAYS.
#
# It needs no audio side and no socket: every record here is a document edit.
#
# The engine came up on the minimal bundle beside it.
A 0 0 engine audio.editBuilt s:"hosted" i:8 i:2 i:36
#
# ONE FIELD, TWICE, FAR ENOUGH APART TO BE TWO GESTURES. The coalescing window
# is twenty-five ticks on the same address from the same origin (§14.9), and
# these are sixty apart: two transactions, two steps to take back.
A 40 1 udp:10.0.0.5:9000 node.set s:"/godot/cue/B3N8R5TW/name" s:"House to full"
A 100 2 udp:10.0.0.5:9000 node.set s:"/godot/cue/B3N8R5TW/name" s:"Houselights out"
#
# AND WITHIN THE WINDOW, from the same origin and the same address: a drag,
# which is ONE step however many values it sent. Three records, one transaction
# - and the undo below proves it by taking all three back at once.
A 140 3 udp:10.0.0.5:9000 node.set s:"/godot/cue/F7HR8TVD/postWait" s:"2"
A 150 4 udp:10.0.0.5:9000 node.set s:"/godot/cue/F7HR8TVD/postWait" s:"2.5"
A 160 5 udp:10.0.0.5:9000 node.set s:"/godot/cue/F7HR8TVD/postWait" s:"3"
#
# UNDO, and its applied arguments are the domain and the transaction's own name
# - the command that opened it. A client puts that word after "Undo".
A 200 6 cli undo s:"document" s:"node.set"
#
# REDO puts the same transaction back, and says so the same way.
A 210 7 cli redo s:"document" s:"node.set"
#
# A CREATE IS ITS OWN STEP, named after itself, and the identifier it draws is
# in the record because a replay must not draw its own.
A 250 8 udp:10.0.0.5:9000 cue.create s:"D9FH2JKA" i:2 s:"memo" s:"To be undone" s:"2R4QMT5H"
#
# Taken back: the cue goes, and the identifier goes back to the registry.
A 300 9 cli undo s:"document" s:"cue.create"
#
# A DELETE OF A GROUP, undone whole. The group carries two cues, and what comes
# back carries them with their own identifiers - which is the case the plan
# named and the unit suite checks object by object.
A 350 10 udp:10.0.0.5:9000 object.delete s:"D9FH2JKA"
A 400 11 cli undo s:"document" s:"object.delete"
#
# THE POINTER IS NOT AN EDIT (§14.9, plan decision 3). A standby move is a state
# row, which no history carries: the undo after it takes back the rename above
# and not the pointer.
A 420 12 udp:10.0.0.5:9000 standby.set s:"B3N8R5TW"
A 440 13 cli undo s:"document" s:"node.set"
#
# THE REST OF THE STACK, taken back one gesture at a time: the drag above was
# one step, and the two renames before it are the two under it. Three undos
# reach the bottom, because five edit records went in as three steps - which is
# the arithmetic the coalescing window decides, and the reason this file counts
# them out loud.
A 460 14 cli undo s:"document" s:"node.set"
A 480 15 cli undo s:"document" s:"node.set"
#
# THE STACK RUNS OUT, and that is a refusal with its own reason rather than a
# command that quietly does nothing.
R 500 16 cli nothing-to-undo undo
#
# AND A LOCKED SHOW REFUSES IT (§14.11). The lock is a state row written like
# any other node, so locking is not itself undoable - and unlocking gets
# through, or the lock could never be lifted.
A 550 17 udp:10.0.0.5:9000 node.set s:"/godot/document/locked" s:"true"
R 560 18 cli locked undo
R 570 19 cli locked redo
A 580 20 udp:10.0.0.5:9000 node.set s:"/godot/document/locked" s:"false"
#
# With the lock lifted, redo works again: the history survived the refusals
# untouched, which is what makes a refusal a refusal.
A 600 21 cli redo s:"document" s:"node.set"
